---
import PageContainer from "../components/layout/PageContainer.astro";
import ContentSection from "../components/ui/ContentSection.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  heading="A brief autobiography"
  description="Some more details about myself."
>
  <PageContainer class="space-y-6">
    <ContentSection id="background" title="Background">
      <p>
        I’m a Computer Science and Mathematics Joint Honours Co-op student at
        the University of Manitoba, minoring in Statistics. I was born and
        raised in Winnipeg, and my choice of degree has always been driven by
        passion: I enjoy the rigour of mathematics and the process of turning an
        idea into a working implementation.
      </p>
      <p>
        My interest in computing began with programming in high school and grew
        into a broader curiosity about how computers work, from the logic of
        algorithms to the design of operating systems.
      </p>
      <p>
        Id like to work in scientific computing (like numerical analysis or
        computational programming) or low-level systems programming (either
        embedded software or operating system kernels). Id also like to dig
        deeper into high-performance parallel computing, as it seems like a
        great field to find intersections in scientific computing and systems
        programming. Perhaps in optimizing existing processes? I aim to find
        out!
      </p>
    </ContentSection>

    <ContentSection id="interests" title="Technical interests">
      <p>
        My main academic interests include discrete algorithms, computational
        geometry, and scientific computing. On the systems side, I’m interested
        in low-level programming, with particular interest in operating systems.
      </p>
      <p>
        I love moving between theory and implementation: analyzing a problem on
        paper and developing an optimized algorithm on paper, proving why it
        works, and then implementing it and running experiments. I have worked
        with Java, Python, C/C#/C++, JavaScript, LaTeX, Linux, and Julia. My IDE
        of choice is Neovim.
      </p>
    </ContentSection>

    <ContentSection id="research-and-teaching" title="Research and teaching">
      <p>
        In Summer 2025, I researched a problem in computational geometry and
        discrete optimization with Dr. Stephane Durocher at the University of
        Manitoba. I also enjoy teaching mathematics, whether in tutorials, the
        Math Help Centre, or an informal conversation about an interesting
        problem. This experience really sparked an interest in theoretical
        research, and motivated me to try researching something more
        mathematically rigorous.
      </p>
      <p>
        In Summer 2026, I contributed to research regarding orthogonal
        polynomials under the supervision of Dr. Mikael Slevinsky at the
        University of Manitoba. The work ranged from analyzing and optimizing
        algorithms to implementing and running experiments in Julia. My interest
        in scientific computing developed here, and I hope to further explore
        the field throughout the rest of my degree.
      </p>
    </ContentSection>
    <ContentSection id="industry" title="Industry experience">
      <p>
        In Winter 2026, I was lucky enough to intern at Conquest Planning for
        four months. It was so much fun working on real-life problems in code
        and presenting my solutions to others on the team. Before this work
        term, I was quite certain I didnt want to enter software development
        roles after graduation, but this experience really shed light on how
        enjoyable these roles can be. Im open to work for Summer 2026 as well,
        so feel free to reach out if you're interested in having me!
      </p>
    </ContentSection>

    <ContentSection id="outside-work" title="Outside work">
      <p>
        Away from coursework and projects, I like reading, weight-lifting,
        refining my Linux environment, and spending time with friends. I hope to
        record any work I’m most proud of on this website, and perhaps document
        what I want to learn next.
      </p>
      <p>
        At the moment, Im still working on becoming better at cooking. Ive
        definitely come far in terms of cooking ability over the past year, but
        Id like to become more experienced in working with uncommon combinations
        of ingredients.
      </p>
      <p>
        Im also working through Fundamentals of Physics, Extended, 12th Edition
        by Halliday, Resni and Walker. Im still quite early into the book, but
        its a very fun time! I wanted to learn physics from the very beginning,
        up to second or third-year university. From what I can tell, this
        behemoth of a book seems to cover every facet of that goal, and perhaps
        more!
      </p>
    </ContentSection>
  </PageContainer>
</BaseLayout>
